{"text": "NEIL\n\nASSOCIATE SALES MANAGER\n\nAccomplished professional with 10 years\nof Sales and Account Management\nexperience. Skilled at developing strong\nvalue propositions for products and\nservices across different industries.\nExceptional client relationships; a\ntrack record of exceeding sales targets;\nowns the full \"customer life cycle.\"\n\n* Results-Oriented\n* Reliable\n* Organized\n* Driven\n* Disciplined\n+ Natural Leader\n* Strong Interpersonal Skills\n* Collaborator\n* Driven to Succeed\n* Customer Service Oriented\n* Proven Enlistment Abilities\n* Compassionate\n* Good Listener\n* Mobile Within Canada\n\nACHIEVEMENTS\nRTA School of Media: Media Production (BA),\nRyerson University, Toronto, 2008\n\nSelected as a Judge/CARAS Academy Delegate for\nthe JUNO Awards 2018\n\nNominated for two Independent Web Creators of\nCanada awards, and for a Canadian Comedy Award\nfor \"Best Audio Show or Series\" 2017-2019\n\nVolunteer Charity Organizer \"Freedom of Comedy\nProtest\" raising funds for local causes (BLM,\nKorchinski-Paquet & Ciasullo families)\n\n\"Address\"\n\"Phone Number\"\n\"Email\"\n\"Website\"\n\"LinkedIn\"\n\nASSOCIATE SALES MANAGER,\nNATIONAL ENTERTAINMENT COMPANY\n\n2019 - Present (furloughed in March due to COVID)\n\n+ Individually generated $350K in national sales revenue in my first year\nand generated jobs for over 75 nation-wide entertainers\n* Executed contracts for entertainment purchasers: 100+ corporate\naccounts; 12 franchised venues; and over 50 independent touring venues\n* Designed engaging events unique to private fundraising campaigns; alcohol\ncompanies (craft beer festivals); and corporate entertainment (national\nbanks; team building events; employee appreciation)\n* Completed successful marketing and communication strategies to fulfill\nticket sale goals and enhance promotional reach\n\nSALES ACCOUNT MANAGER,\nARCHITECTURAL SALES COMPANY\n\n2013 - 2016\n* Cultivated B2B accounts for an architectural and design firm generating\n$1M in commercial, institutional, and residential sales revenue\n- Performed high-impact presentations to coordinate meetings and network\nwith architects, engineers, and interior designers while delivering\ncompelling sales opportunities\n- Established a variety of new transferable skills such as, grasping\ngovernment code policies, creating virtual sales decks, and evolving my\nmarketing and design knowledge to assist current and prospective clients\n\nINDEPENDENT MEDIA PRODUCER,\nLOCAL PODCAST NETWORK\n\n2012 - Present\n* Media production freelancer specializing in podcast production; talent\nmanagement; social media content creation; and sponsorship acquisition\n* Developed diverse national content with over 1M social media\nimpressions and 353K followers across all show and host platforms\n+ Featured in NOW Magazine, Metro News, and The Canadian Jewish News\n\nAUDIENCE & INTERN COORDINATOR/SOCIAL MEDIA MANAGER,\nNATIONAL BROADCASTER\n\n2011-2012\n+ Coordinated & supervised audiences of up to 200 ticket holders, for\nbroadcasting network events and live tapings\n+ Engaged the audience\u2019s digital interactions on various social networks\nusing original copywriting and unique campaigns\n+ Managed a team of 20 interns during live shows and events",
